WEBVTT

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:06.360
If Onoda makes it through the 
blockade and catches up to the team,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.650
send him to the front if he's less 
than three and a half minutes behind.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.390
Onoda's strong enough to 
catch up to the front.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.280
But if it's more than that...

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.870
You can't catch up to the front.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.450
It's already been four and a half.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.460
No matter how hard you pedal, you may not 
even catch a glimpse of Teshima-san's back.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.380
Do you still want to go?

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.630
Yeah.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.010
Take them to him, Sakamichi!

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.120
Yes, sir!

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.160
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.960
<i>RIDE.24 The Ride of Weeds</i>

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:12.960
Manami Sangaku.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:19.990
Racing you and taking the first day's
 mountain number tag is my job!

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.580
I'm starting to get interested.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:28.080
<i>Without Onoda, the only 
climber we could send was me.</i>

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:29.830
<i>So...</i>

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.590
<i>I'll take the mountain number tag!</i>

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.240
You can do it!

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.640
Sohoku High School's in front!

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.430
On the winding roads of Irohazaka?
That's amazing!

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.310
But Hakone Academy High School's 
rider seems more composed.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.430
Is he smiling?

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.930
He's letting #5 get in front of him!

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.460
Are you okay, Teshima-san?

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.290
Are you sure you're not pushing yourself 
too hard by keeping up that high pace?

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.360
I am.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.930
But I'm racing against you.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:00.290
It's worth it.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.450
I'm honored.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:06.540
<i>He's fast. He caught up in a second.</i>

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.290
Mind if I ride alongside you?

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.300
What are we doing, sitting on a park bench?

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.920
Want to switch places?

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.790
We just ran into a headwind.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.960
No, we'll keep going like this.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.840
Once we make it through the next turn,
I'll move to the front.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:25.730
After all, the wind will change directions.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:26.760
A tailwind?

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:29.850
<i>Crap!</i>

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:33.280
<i>The wind direction changes on 
each turn on a zigzagging road.</i>

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.230
<i>Manami Sangaku's planning to use his wings.</i>

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.150
The wind's coming.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.490
<i>If I don't get ahead of 
him now, he'll catch up.</i>

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.870
<i>If he does...</i>

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.880
Coming through.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.920
I feel alive.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.100
It feels awesome.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.850
<i>If he does...</i>

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.190
Teshima went?

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.790
What happened to Onoda?

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.930
Hakone Academy High School sent Manami-kun.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:22.860
Manami?

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.460
Is he strong?

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:26.310
Is that Manami guy bad news?

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:30.120
He's the climber we fought 
at the finish line last year.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.100
Yikes. That guy?

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:34.500
But Teshima-san's strong, too, right?

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.410
He's the captain.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.820
<i>Is that role too heavy for you, Teshima?</i>

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.880
Hey, why isn't anyone talking?

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.330
Did you guys give up?

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.260
I haven't given up.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:53.090
M-Manami's just a little fast!

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.440
Who cares about Hakone?

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.940
We've practiced a lot, too.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:58.830
Sugimoto-san...

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:02.690
Teshima-san always states the obvious.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:05.870
Don't apply any unnecessary 
force to your pedals.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.450
Yes, sir. I know.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:13.200
Sugimoto, you'll get there faster if 
you climb stairs one step at a time.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.410
I saw that on TV.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:19.470
Your muscles last longer 
than if you skip steps.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.590
I know. It's obvious.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.100
Even I know.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:27.220
But he's the kind of person who puts

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.310
each and every one of those 
obvious facts into practice.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.640
<i>Don't let your pedaling waver 
when you're struggling.</i>

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.480
<i>I'm an ordinary guy.</i>

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:43.400
<i>I don't have power. I don't 
have flashes of inspiration.</i>

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:48.660
<i>That's why I have to convert all 
of my strength into forward thrust.</i>

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:50.980
<i>The fundamentals are important.</i>

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:53.060
<i>Everything stands on them.</i>

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:56.660
<i>It would suck if he caught up to me.</i>

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.880
Actually, he already passed me.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:04.380
<i>Catching up to him again will be hard.</i>

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.810
Wait, Manami.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:15.850
What's the hurry?

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:18.850
I thought your spirit broke 
when I passed you earlier.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.860
You don't have to force yourself to keep up.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.360
It's just like your wings.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.110
Pushing myself too hard 
is my strongest technique.

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:32.610
Your body is screaming.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.950
Want to try me?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.160
Are your hands numb?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.000
They're trembling with excitement.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.670
That's promising.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.630
I guess I'll start, too...

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.880
Going all out.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.180
<i>Don't lose it.</i>

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.730
<i>Don't lose focus,</i>

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.150
<i>Teshima Junta!</i>

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:07.800
Go!

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:10.700
So fast!

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.220
<i>It's hard.</i>

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:16.330
<i>I feel like all my pores are 
about to start bleeding.</i>

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:19.290
<i>Endure it. Endure it.</i>

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:23.610
<i>He's trying to break away from me.</i>

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:26.050
<i>If he breaks away now, it's over.</i>

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.710
<i>Endure it.</i>

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:31.430
<i>He's fast. Manami's fast.</i>

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:36.600
<i>Is this the full strength of
Hakone Academy High School's ace climber?</i>

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:48.220
<i>Come to think of it, I made that shot into 
the trash can during class the other day.</i>

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:51.860
<i>My neighbor Hirata thought it was great.</i>

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:56.330
<i>I think Hirata said she has a sister.</i>

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.450
Whew.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:01.630
Nothing beats the moment you fall 
into bed after finishing practice,

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:04.290
taking a bath, and eating dinner.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:08.230
Since I don't have any assignments tonight,
I might fall asleep like this.

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:11.050
Someone turn out the lights.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:13.840
My bed feels good.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.760
I don't have to move.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.010
I can forget all my pain.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.180
<i>Beds are the best.</i>

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:32.310
<i>What are you doing, Teshima Junta?</i>

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.950
<i>You're in the middle of a race!</i>

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.240
He pushed himself back up 
when he started to fall.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:40.170
He might have lost 
consciousness for a second.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:40.950
What?

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:44.710
Your brain turns off under 
brutal circumstances.

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:48.340
<i>I told you not to lose focus!</i>

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.840
<i>I can barely keep up. I'm at my limit.</i>

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.630
You seem to be struggling.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.600
You're lucky, Teshima-san.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.720
This is enough to make you feel alive.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:00.970
I only feel like I'm dead,

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:04.310
Manami!

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.350
Isn't this starting to get fun, Teshima-san?

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:14.110
Is your focus heightened, too, Manami?

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.870
It is.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:19.870
I wasn't expecting today's 
mountains to be this much fun.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.600
You're at your limit, but you're keeping up.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:24.500
You're not flashy.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:26.500
You're not strong.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.450
Leave me alone.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:29.750
Come to think of it...

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:33.010
But I always arrive at the same answer.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:36.200
What's your "one answer"?

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:37.600
You were listening?

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:39.520
Is it because you're the captain?

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:41.390
Because you're a third-year?

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:44.820
You accelerated before 
I was finished talking.

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:46.950
I wasn't interested then.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.480
Is it because you wear a 
single-digit number tag?

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:53.980
<i>His question was so direct, I laughed.</i>

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:59.370
No. It's simpler than that.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:01.160
I...

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.620
I love bikes.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:09.420
They always take you to your destination.
That's why I ride.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.650
I chase. I pedal.

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:14.020
I help.

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:15.550
I believe in miracles.

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:21.700
After I started racing, I thought
about quitting, since I'd never place first.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:26.350
But I met a guy named Aoyagi and 
realized that wasn't everything.

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:33.730
I met the bespectacled Onoda,
the giant Imaizumi, and the red Naruko.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:39.030
Seeing them and a bunch of others ride,
I learned something.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:43.230
Even if the going gets rough and you 
want to quit, you have to stay strong.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:49.500
They're all connected through bicycles.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:54.340
I think Onoda said something similar.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:57.160
Is your plan to have Sakamichi-kun come?

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:00.230
Do you think you can win 
the mountains like that?

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:11.480
Wouldn't it be all right if 
even I placed first, just once?

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:15.020
It's what I secretly think.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:22.260
He left right away.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.710
Sohoku High School's Onoda...

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:27.730
Despite being small,
his pressure was amazing.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:29.230
They're wasting their time.

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:33.130
He's too far behind. Even if 
he goes, he can't catch up.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.290
The race will come down to those two...

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:39.690
Manami and Teshima-kun.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:45.300
<i>If it's actually a race, that is.</i>

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:48.350
<i>That's it.</i>

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:52.560
<i>He went to save Teshima,
who's surely about to drop out.</i>

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:55.390
<i>So he's just the rescue team?</i>

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.890
You can do it!

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:02.140
It's amazing that you're still keeping up.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:03.860
Just how stubborn are you?

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:08.270
I'll stick with you until 
the mountain result line.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.120
That's why I'm riding.

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:15.050
There's three kilometers left to the line.

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:19.380
It doesn't look like Sakamichi-kun is coming.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.150
Don't worry.

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:24.340
I gave up hope that he would 
at the four kilometer mark.

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:28.100
So you're challenging me to 
a one-on-one mountain race.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.710
That's what I've been saying.

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:32.890
Then it's on.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:36.450
The end of Irohazaka lies 
three kilometers ahead

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:39.500
at the mountain result line of the 
Akechidaira observation platform.

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:45.410
If you're unhappy with your opponent,
you'd better say so now.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:49.100
Even I'd be depressed if you 
told me after this is over.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:52.640
No, I said plenty when we started.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.730
But now I feel differently.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:59.450
This is the first time I've 
encountered someone like you.

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:03.340
Most people give up after 
falling behind a couple times.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.670
But you don't give up, no matter 
how many times I trample you.

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:08.430
You're like a summer weed.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.930
That's not a compliment.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.180
That's why I feel this way.

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:16.940
If I don't ride as hard 
as I can, it'd be a waste.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:19.820
What?

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.570
Go!

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:24.750
He shifted up a gear on a climb!

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:25.780
He's so fast!

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.160
Sohoku High School's #5 is keeping up!

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:33.130
I can't believe he accelerated 
on the steep part of Irohazaka.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:36.080
Manami is a natural climber, too.

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:42.840
But isn't that guy keeping up 
with him the most amazing of all?

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:46.930
They should be coming up on 
the mountain result line.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:51.140
Anyway, I was surprised 
when Teshima-san left.

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:56.580
He's up against their mountain ace.
He doesn't stand a chance.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:58.420
He always talks about how weak he is.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:01.940
I thought Imaizumi-san should've gone, too.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:06.020
You don't understand, Kaburagi.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:10.820
Junta left because he knows he's weak.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:12.780
What?

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:16.040
If Imaizumi had gone, Ashikiba would've gone.

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:19.370
If Naruko had gone,
Kuroda would've gone after him.

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:21.750
But Junta is different.

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:24.930
He knew Hakone Academy High School 
wouldn't send someone after him,

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:27.670
because they believe Manami 
would be enough to stop him.

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:29.930
It was on purpose?

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.650
That was on purpose?

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:34.490
Does that mean this was all 
part of Teshima-san's plan?

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:38.370
Seriously? Teshima-san is amazing.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:43.640
He might have some plan for 
beating Manami-san, too.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:44.940
A plan?

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:49.460
Probably not.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:52.870
Manami!

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:58.780
<i>I'm struggling so much, 
I can't raise my head.</i>

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:01.250
<i>My hands are full trying 
to follow his wheels.</i>

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:05.710
<i>Don't fall behind.
Please don't fall behind, wheels.</i>

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:10.180
<i>If I don't stay right on the line,
I won't stand a chance.</i>

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:12.770
<i>I don't care if my legs fall apart.</i>

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:14.690
<i>I don't care if I lose consciousness.</i>

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:17.330
<i>Three kilometers left.</i>

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:23.380
<i>Until I cross the line, 
let my body keep moving!</i>

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:30.360
<i>But the calmer side of me says this.</i>

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:36.990
<i>"Teshima Junta, three years ago,
you quit road racing."</i>

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:43.130
<i>"Now you're fighting for first in the 
glorious mountain stage of the Inter-High."</i>

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:49.010
<i>Surely it's all right
for a crownless man like me</i>

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:52.910
<i>to win just once.</i>

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.730
It's strange, Teshima-san.

00:15:56.730 --> 00:16:01.480
Your riding has been sharper since you 
realized Sakamichi-kun isn't coming.

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.480
I wonder why.

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:07.410
<i>My body does feel lighter.</i>

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.470
<i>Maybe it's because 
I realized I have to do it.</i>

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:14.430
<i>Maybe it's because I'm 
carrying my teammates' hopes.</i>

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:19.870
You said you gave up hope earlier,
but you never had hope.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:24.070
<i>He might be right. I don't have hope.</i>

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:27.750
<i>All I can do is move forward one step
 at a time with my own two legs.</i>

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:32.220
<i>It's what I've always done.</i>

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:33.750
You can do it!

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:37.430
<i>In a few kilometers,
my efforts will be rewarded.</i>

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:42.680
<i>I may be able to experience that moment.</i>

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:47.570
Road racing really is fun.
Right, Teshima-san?

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:49.410
Yeah, you're right.

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.070
It's fun, Manami.

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:56.100
That's the first time you agreed with me.

00:16:56.100 --> 00:16:59.530
Of course riding a bike is fun!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:04.220
It's Yamagata Mogami High School,
who was riding alone!

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:10.170
They passed the favorite to win 
the mountains, Kawahara Gunpei!

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:13.670
Now Hakone Academy High School and
Sohoku High School are racing for first!

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:17.790
<i>There's nothing to get in our 
way anymore, Teshima-san.</i>

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:20.100
<i>Was he planning to pass him here?</i>

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:23.870
<i>Were they going for the result?</i>

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:27.440
<i>But Sohoku High School's #5 was behind him.</i>

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:33.070
<i>I thought Sohoku High School's ace was 
the guy I told Bunya to keep in check.</i>

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:36.610
<i>Number 5 flew under my radar.</i>

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:42.060
<i>I meant to take the first day's mountain 
result by riding ahead of the others.</i>

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:44.910
<i>But I couldn't react.</i>

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:49.400
<i>Normally, I should've been able to follow 
them and fight until the finish line.</i>

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:51.320
<i>I'm sorry, Bunya.</i>

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:53.840
<i>You did your job, too.</i>

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:58.970
<i>But there are demons at the Inter-High.</i>

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:04.020
<i>Demons who turn birds flying 
in the sky into pebbles.</i>

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:09.020
<i>And demons who turn 
ordinary pebbles into birds.</i>

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.970
<i>The Inter-High is a special race.</i>

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:17.490
<i>Will, responsibility, tension, 
and purpose mix together.</i>

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:20.950
<i>You can't move like you normally do here.</i>

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:27.460
<i>With the second type of demon on 
your side, you have nothing to fear.</i>

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:32.770
<i>Could it be that #5 is...</i>

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:39.480
<i>A chance, a chance...</i>

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:40.930
<i>Search for a chance.</i>

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:43.640
<i>Fifteen hundred meters left.</i>

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:48.280
<i>I can't win if I keep riding behind Manami.</i>

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:51.910
<i>I have to pass him somewhere.</i>

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:53.080
<i>On the way?</i>

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.530
<i>Before the finish line? Now?</i>

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:58.150
<i>I can't miss the tiniest of mistakes.</i>

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:00.770
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:03.620
<i>Whoa!</i>

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:06.080
Damn it, I fell behind!

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.690
<i>There's no way he'd make a mistake.</i>

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:11.820
<i>If anyone makes one, it'll be me.</i>

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:13.330
<i>So what should I do?</i>

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:16.420
<i>Twelve hundred meters left...</i>

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:19.300
You're keeping up.
You're keeping up, Teshima-san!

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.640
I keep shifting up.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.260
<i>He shifted up again?</i>

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:26.890
<i>This isn't an opportunity, it's a disaster.</i>

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.600
<i>Is he trying to kill me?</i>

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:34.280
<i>One kilometer left!</i>

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:35.680
<i>The line...</i>

00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:36.480
<i>is close!</i>

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.570
<i>Find an opportunity.</i>

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:41.790
<i>One kilometer left...</i>

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:44.490
<i>Just one kilometer in a lifetime.</i>

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.530
<i>I'll take first.</i>

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:52.420
<i>It's right in front of me!</i>

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.750
<i>My legs are at their limit.</i>

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:59.130
<i>My hands are losing their grip.</i>

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.490
<i>But they've been that way for a while.</i>

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:04.910
<i>Believe in yourself!</i>

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:06.890
<i>In miracles!</i>

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.370
#5 is amazing!

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:10.610
He's giving Manami a run for his money!

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:12.770
Teshima!

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:16.520
I kind of like all-out, reckless riders like him!

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:15.790
Teshima!

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:17.990
Teshima-san!

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:18.460
You can do it, Sohoku High School!

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:20.320
Take it, Teshima!

00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:22.430
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:24.030
Teshima, go!

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:28.250
<i>I can hear my name being 
called at the Inter-High.</i>

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:30.410
<i>Is this a miracle?</i>

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:33.330
<i>I feel stronger.</i>

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:37.840
You're almost at the end of Irohazaka!

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:02.570
<i>Crap! My chain!</i>

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:04.610
<i>Manami's losing speed?</i>

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:05.640
<i>What happened?</i>

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:06.910
<i>In any case...</i>

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:09.910
Now's my chance!

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:12.900
Sohoku High School passed him!

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:14.910
There's 400 meters left!

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:54.690
I can't keep going.

00:22:54.690 --> 00:22:56.850
I can't move another millimeter.

00:22:56.850 --> 00:22:58.430
I'm going to sleep here.

00:22:58.430 --> 00:22:59.800
What about dinner?

00:22:59.800 --> 00:23:01.710
I'm not hungry.

00:23:01.710 --> 00:23:03.940
We ordinary men have reached their limit.

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:05.230
Good night.

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:08.690
Junta, you completed a thousand 
kilometers at this training camp.

00:23:09.310 --> 00:23:10.700
You're not ordinary anymore.

00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:13.070
Aoyagi...

00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:17.120
Yeah. If you're ordinary, 
what does that make me?

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:20.230
You're a proper captain now.

00:23:20.820 --> 00:23:22.580
I'm counting on you at the Inter-High.

00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:23.810
Kimitaka...

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:27.490
Okay, time for dinner!

00:23:27.490 --> 00:23:29.800
We'll start without you, Junta!

00:23:33.630 --> 00:23:36.200
I really am ordinary.

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:39.890
<i>NEXT RIDE  Look Up At The Sky</i>

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:44.900
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.
